> **Judges: start here.** The paper is [`docs/NOTE.pdf`](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZMOhVQHA-lSsqmIboTntavcxZIRGt4Nr/view) ({{meta:main_pages}} pages + references and
> appendix, 11 pt, 1 in margins). The video is [`results/viz/courtside_60.mp4`](results/viz/courtside_60.mp4)
> ({{meta:video_s}} s). Devpost text: [`docs/DEVPOST.md`](docs/DEVPOST.md). Rules checklist: [`docs/COMPLIANCE.md`](docs/COMPLIANCE.md).
>
> **Quick path (about 10 minutes, no data download, no keys).** Run from the repo root; tested on Python 3.12 (Linux)
> and 3.14 (macOS).
>
> | Command | What it does | Time |
> |---|---|---|
> | `bash run.sh setup` | makes `.venv`, installs `requirements-repro.txt` (`requirements.txt` plus duckdb, paramiko, tabulate and OpenCV, which `reproduce` needs; `--locked` installs the exact versions in `requirements.lock`) and finds the paper compiler (tectonic 0.17.0 from `PATH`, `TECTONIC=/path`, or `INSTALL_TECTONIC=1` for the official release binary) | ~1–2 min |
> | `bash run.sh replay` | 10 min of recorded live Polymarket books (`tests/fixtures/live_sample.jsonl.gz`, public data) through the paper trader and the engine's order books; no network. Like every replay it appends one line to the tracked `results/oos_peeks.log` (`git checkout results/oos_peeks.log` undoes it) | ~15 s |
> | `bash run.sh redteam` | the checks we ran against ourselves: stamp-lag robustness, every derived number from its results file, claim checks on the paper, deck, docs and the final video's script and subtitles (`results/redteam/`); no network, no held-out read. Expected: 0 FAIL; KNOWN = a gap in the final video (not re-rendered); NOT RUN = the forward test (`HYPOTHESIS_V2.md` A5) | ~10 s |
> | `bash run.sh tests` | unit tests (vision tests too after `bash run.sh setup --full`) | ~2–7 min |
> | `bash run.sh docs` | rebuilds this README, `docs/DEVPOST.md` and `docs/COMPLIANCE.md` from `results/paper/numbers.json` and the paper's label map (`results/paper/labels.json` on a clone); writes nothing if any placeholder does not resolve | ~1 s |
>
> **Reproduce the submitted snapshot, one command:** `bash run.sh all` (setup, the public Polymarket crawl, then
> `reproduce.sh`). The crawl took 35 min on 16 CPUs (no keys, resumable); `reproduce.sh` takes about 1–1.5 h and
> peaks near 12 GB of memory. `reproduce.sh` first checks the crawled inputs against
> [`results/provenance/inputs_manifest.json`](results/provenance/inputs_manifest.json) (universe, 80/20 split, OOS
> start, the sha256 of every trade tape, the frozen call model) and stops on a mismatch; it then reruns every step
> offline, fails on the first error, and writes `results/repro/run_manifest.json`. Paper numbers it does not
> recompute (HiPerGator jobs, recorded live books, blind tests evaluated once) are listed file by file, with
> producer, sha256 and reason, in [`results/paper/committed_artifacts.json`](results/paper/committed_artifacts.json).
> `bash run.sh fresh-fetch` is the separate, mutable path: it fetches a new holdout from today's listing into its own
> directory. Clean-clone status: [`research/compliance/CLEAN_CLONE.md`](research/compliance/CLEAN_CLONE.md).
>
> **Check any number:** all {{meta:n_numbers}} numbers in the paper are in `results/paper/numbers.json`, each with
> the results file and key it came from. Every number below is read from that file when this README is built.
>
> - Paper only: no real money, and nothing here signs or sends an order. We bought no licensed data feed and have no
>   match video: the CV strategy is simulated at an **assumed** feed latency (licensed feed not purchased); its
>   parameters are measured. Free public score pages (ESPN, WTA) were recorded only to time their lag.
> - A fresh clone has no market data (`data/` is gitignored): `bash run.sh data` comes before `reproduce` or `money`.
> - The CV point-end calls use `models/vision/frozen_call_model.pkl` (12 MB, committed). `bash run.sh cv` checks its
>   sha256 against the input manifest and stops if it is missing or different; `sbatch hpg/engine_vision.sbatch`
>   (HiPerGator) rebuilt it.
> - Footage: the table-tennis clips are OpenTTGames (OSAI) footage, adapted (overlays added), CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The
>   video's real tennis rally is {{meta:tennis_credit}}, shown with the tracked ball trail (public TrackNet detector, our linking) and no line calls; it is
>   not a match we traded. The video's narration and music bed are AI-generated with {{meta:voice}}.
> - `bash run.sh help` lists every command with its run time.

# COURTSIDE

**Who gets paid in the seconds after a tennis point, and what it takes to be first.**
Ojasva Mishra · Yoan Exposito · Rafael Penhas · Ian Hoang · University of Florida.
Gator Quant Hacks 2026 · Systematic Trading track · Paper: [`docs/NOTE.pdf`](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZMOhVQHA-lSsqmIboTntavcxZIRGt4Nr/view)
("COURTSIDE: Calling the Point Before It Lands. Predictive Ball Tracking and the Value of Speed in In-Play Tennis Markets").

Every tennis point moves a prediction market. On every resolved Polymarket ATP/WTA singles moneyline
from {{univ.first}} to {{univ.last}} ({{univ.matches}} matches, {{univ.volume}} traded) we measured who makes and who
loses money in the seconds after each point. Then we priced the speed a computer-vision (CV) trader would need to
join the winners. The answer: speed is the edge, and the break-even feed delay is the result.

## Results

Same numbers and labels as the paper (location in brackets). IS = in sample; OOS = the held-out last
{{univ.oos}} matches from {{univ.oosstart}} (20% of matches, pre-registered; {{split.oos_days}} days, {{univ.oos_time}} of
the calendar, so it does not meet the organizers' latest-20%-by-time rule), opened once, blind, for v1 and
**non-blind** for v2, the copier and the CV policies, which were designed after it was read. ¢ = net cents per share after each match's own fee. Executable
results (what we could run at our latency, net of costs) come first; v2 (the fast tier's own fills) and the CV trader
(trades only on points the price later moved) are labelled benchmarks, not returns we could earn.

| | Result |
|---|---|
| **Executable: a copier** (v2's trades printed after the detection second, filled after the venue's hold and the {{copier.lag}} s block lag, net of costs) | Loses: {{copier.is.usd}} / {{copier.oos.usd}} a day, {{copier.is.c}}¢ {{copier.is.ci}} / {{copier.oos.c}}¢ {{copier.oos.ci}} a share, Sharpe {{copier.is.sr}} / {{copier.oos.sr}} (IS / OOS). A replay of {{rp.matches}} live-recorded matches' real books, calling every point at the pre-registered 2 s stamp lag, loses {{rp.v05l2.c}}¢ {{rp.v05l2.ci}} at a 0.5 s feed and {{rp.v1l2.c}}¢ {{rp.v1l2.ci}} at 1 s ({{rp.cells_neg}} of {{rp.cells}} settings below zero). [Table {{ref:tab:head}}] |
| **The edge** (fast tier: wallets trading ≤ 3 s after a score move, chosen walk-forward on past months) | {{ft.c.is}}¢ / {{ft.c.oos.only}}¢ a share after fees (IS / OOS prints only; {{ft.c.oos}}¢ if August's IS prints are included), positive in **{{ft.months.is}} IS and {{ft.months.oos}} OOS months** ({{video:ft_pos}} of {{video:ft_n}} calendar months, as in the video). Other takers lose ({{oth.c.is}}¢ / {{oth.c.oos}}¢); copying the same trades 3 s later loses ({{copy3.c.is}}¢ / {{copy3.c.oos}}¢). Chasing the move after a point (H1) loses {{h1.is.c}}¢ / {{h1.oos.c}}¢. [Fig. {{ref:fig:edge}}a] |
| **Benchmark: v2** (frozen book at the fast tier's own fills, an event study; sizing `{{sel.sizing.pick}}`, 100-share net cap, hold to resolution; {{decay.sameblock.share}} of its profit is in trades stamped in the same block as the score move that selects them) | IS: Sharpe **{{v2.is.sr}}** {{v2.is.sr_ci}}, {{v2.is.c}}¢ {{v2.is.ci}}, deflated Sharpe {{v2.is.dsr}}, max DD {{v2.is.dd}}, {{v2.is.mpos}} months. **OOS (non-blind):** Sharpe **{{v2.oos.sr}}** {{v2.oos.sr_ci}}, {{v2.oos.c}}¢ {{v2.oos.ci}}, deflated Sharpe {{v2.oos.dsr}} (at {{rig.N3386}} trials); turnover {{v2.is.turnover}} / {{v2.oos.turnover}}× capital a year; {{v2.oos.slip05}}¢ at ½ tick worse entry; **negative with costs doubled** (fees ×2 {{v2.oos.fx2.c}}¢, all costs ×2 {{v2.oos.cx2.c}}¢). PSR, MinTRL and a haircut over all {{var.total}} variants: 6 of 6 tests pass IS, {{rig2.v2oos.pass}} of 6 OOS (haircut Sharpe {{rig2.v2oos.hlz_sr}}). The opportunity at their speed, not our execution. [Table {{ref:tab:head}}, Fig. {{ref:fig:edge}}b] |
| **Benchmark: a firm with a licensed 0.5 s feed** (counterfactual: real prices, fills and fees, simulated calls on points that later moved, no feed bought) | OOS {{sc.pre.oos.v05.usd}} / {{sc.cal.oos.v05.usd}} a day (pre-registered / post hoc). **Fresh holdout**, pre-registered at `{{fresh.prereg.commit}}` before its data were fetched ({{fresh.covered}} newer matches, {{fresh.days}} UTC days): {{fresh.s2.pre.v05.usd}} / {{fresh.s2.cal.v05.usd}} a day, CIs {{fresh.s2.pre.v05.ci}} and {{fresh.s2.cal.v05.ci}}: anecdotal. Break-even feed price a month: {{fresh.lic.oos.pre}} / {{fresh.lic.oos.cal}} OOS vs quotes of {{fin.feed.low}}–{{fin.feed.high}}. [Fig. {{ref:fig:firm}}] |
| v1 (copy the fast tier, $ sizing) | {{v1.is.c}}¢ IS; **{{v1.oos.usd}}** on the held-out window (opened once, blind). [Table {{ref:tab:A-all}}] |
| v2-safe (net cap 50, fixed after v2's OOS losses) | Sharpe {{v2s.is.sr}} / {{v2s.oos.sr}} (IS / OOS, non-blind); failed its blind unseen-market test ({{v2s.u2.c}}¢ {{v2s.u2.ci}}). [Table {{ref:tab:A-all}}] |
| **Causal camera policy** (every point, calls from the frozen classifier's measured table-tennis call statistics because no footage of these matches exists; simulated, upper-bound fills) | Pre-registered 2.0 s stamp lag, 0.5 / 1 / 3 s feed: {{cvx.is.v05.usd}} / {{cvx.is.v1.usd}} / {{cvx.is.v3.usd}} a day IS, {{cvx.oos.v05.usd}} / {{cvx.oos.v1.usd}} / {{cvx.oos.v3.usd}} OOS; fully pre-registered per-point timing {{cvx.pt.is.v05.usd}} / {{cvx.pt.oos.v05.usd}} at 0.5 s; post hoc 3.14 s lag {{cvx.ph.is.v05.usd}} / {{cvx.ph.oos.v05.usd}} at 0.5 s, {{cvx.ph.oos.v1.usd}} OOS at 1 s. Every cell loses with fees doubled; the {{risk.daily_stop}} daily stop never fired. [Table {{ref:tab:head}}] |
