| CV, tennis (simulated physics) | A spin-aware tracker cuts landing error from {{cv.spin.base200}} to {{cv.spin.bls200}} cm at 200 ms before the bounce, in simulation. Our tennis calls are simulated; the video's real rally (licensed stock footage) shows only the tracked ball trail (public detector, our linking). No tennis match video was used for trading. [Table {{ref:tab:A-all}}] |
| **Capacity** | v2's OOS CI excludes zero only up to 1× size ({{cap.1x.oos.capital}} of capital); 5× loses. The CV book has no capacity at the pre-registered lag (Sharpe {{capcv.pre.sr0.is}} / {{capcv.pre.sr0.oos}} at its smallest size); post hoc its Sharpe halves at {{capcv.half.oos}} (OOS) and {{capcv.half.is}} (IS) of capital. It trades {{capcv.share_inplay}} of in-play volume but {{capcv.share_fast}} of the fast tier's 0–3 s volume. [§{{ref:sec:liq}}, Fig. {{ref:fig:capacity}}] |
| Costs | Fees paid: {{v2.is.fee_bps}} / {{v2.oos.fee_bps}} bps of notional for v2 (IS / OOS), {{cv.fee_bps.range}} bps for the CV trader; with fees doubled every OOS CV cell loses (best {{cv.fx2.oos.best}} a day). Price impact (log in size, fitted on {{liq.orders.fit}} IS orders) cuts v2's 1× OOS from {{liq.v2.1x.oos.none}} to {{liq.v2.1x.oos.central}} a day. v2 OOS after central fixed costs: {{fin.v2.oos.net_central}}/day. At 1 s the CV book can pay at most {{cv.cal.oos.maxlic}} a month for data post hoc and {{cv.pre.oos.maxlic}} pre-registered, against quotes of {{fin.feed.low}}–{{fin.feed.high}}. COURTSIDE prices speed; it is not yet a business. [§{{ref:sec:liq}}, Fig. {{ref:fig:cap}}] |
| Rigour | **{{var.total}} variants in all; {{video:n_trials}} strategy variants (the video's count); {{rig.N3386}} in the deflated Sharpe** (the first adds the sensitivities and grids; the second adds the v2-safe grid to the third). the choices made after an OOS look are listed from `results/provenance/experiments.json` (Appendix {{app:Records}}); PBO {{rig.pbo.lowloss}} and deflated Sharpe {{v2.oos.dsr}} OOS: luck not ruled out out of sample; factor-neutral α t = {{fac.alpha_t}} (max factor \|t\| {{fac.max_t}}). [Table {{ref:tab:A-all}}, Appendices {{app:Calculations}} and {{app:Records}}] |

**Benchmark: the CV strategy at three assumed feed latencies** (simulated; {{meta:label_cv}}). Net $ a day, Sharpe
and ¢ a share [95% CI]; {{cv.seeds}} seeds a cell. The trade set is the historical points the market later repriced by
≥ 4¢, selected on the outcome, so every cell is an upper bound, not an executable return. [Table {{ref:tab:head}}, Fig. {{ref:fig:speed}}]

| Feed latency (assumed) | **Pre-registered** (stamp lag {{cv.pre.lag}} s), IS | **Pre-registered**, OOS | Post hoc estimate ({{cv.cal.lag}} s), IS | Post hoc estimate, OOS |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0.5 s, best case | {{sc.pre.is.v05.usd}}, {{sc.pre.is.v05.sr}}, {{sc.pre.is.v05.c}}¢ {{sc.pre.is.v05.cci}} | {{sc.pre.oos.v05.usd}}, {{sc.pre.oos.v05.sr}}, {{sc.pre.oos.v05.c}}¢ {{sc.pre.oos.v05.cci}} | {{sc.cal.is.v05.usd}}, {{sc.cal.is.v05.sr}}, {{sc.cal.is.v05.c}}¢ {{sc.cal.is.v05.cci}} | {{sc.cal.oos.v05.usd}}, {{sc.cal.oos.v05.sr}}, {{sc.cal.oos.v05.c}}¢ {{sc.cal.oos.v05.cci}} |
| **1 s, base case** | {{sc.pre.is.v1.usd}}, {{sc.pre.is.v1.sr}}, {{sc.pre.is.v1.c}}¢ {{sc.pre.is.v1.cci}} | **{{sc.pre.oos.v1.usd}}**, {{sc.pre.oos.v1.sr}}, {{sc.pre.oos.v1.c}}¢ {{sc.pre.oos.v1.cci}} | {{sc.cal.is.v1.usd}}, {{sc.cal.is.v1.sr}}, {{sc.cal.is.v1.c}}¢ {{sc.cal.is.v1.cci}} | {{sc.cal.oos.v1.usd}}, {{sc.cal.oos.v1.sr}}, {{sc.cal.oos.v1.c}}¢ {{sc.cal.oos.v1.cci}} |
| 3 s, the organisers' bar | {{sc.pre.is.v3.usd}}, {{sc.pre.is.v3.sr}}, {{sc.pre.is.v3.c}}¢ {{sc.pre.is.v3.cci}} | {{sc.pre.oos.v3.usd}}, {{sc.pre.oos.v3.sr}}, {{sc.pre.oos.v3.c}}¢ {{sc.pre.oos.v3.cci}} | {{sc.cal.is.v3.usd}}, {{sc.cal.is.v3.sr}}, {{sc.cal.is.v3.c}}¢ {{sc.cal.is.v3.cci}} | {{sc.cal.oos.v3.usd}}, {{sc.cal.oos.v3.sr}}, {{sc.cal.oos.v3.c}}¢ {{sc.cal.oos.v3.cci}} |
| Break-even feed delay | {{cv.pre.be.is}} s | {{cv.pre.be.oos}} s | {{cv.cal.be.is}} s | {{cv.cal.be.oos}} s |

Read the pre-registered columns first: at the 1 s base case the CV trader breaks even out of sample. The post hoc
stamp lag ({{cv.cal.lag}} s, 95% CI {{cv.cal.lag_ci}} s) assumes the fast tier are courtside humans; at its interval's
low end the OOS cell is only {{cv.at_lo.oos.usd}}/day. At 1 s the same clocks read point by point lose
({{pp.pre.oos.usd}}/day); with no early CV calls the pre-registered OOS cell is {{cv.pess.oos.usd}}/day; and a replay on
{{rp.matches}} matches' real recorded books, calling every point ex ante, loses in {{rp.cells_neg}} of {{rp.cells}}
delay × lag settings ({{rp.v1l2.c}}¢ {{rp.v1l2.ci}} at 1 s). We claim a price on each second of speed, not a bankable
CV P&L. The video's profit scene shows the 1 s post hoc estimate ({{video:lc_is_day}} and {{video:lc_oos_day}} dollars a
day, IS and OOS) with its label, and the pre-registered numbers on its stats rail.

Integrity trail: `HYPOTHESIS.md` (committed before any result, `{{prereg.hyp.commit}}`, {{prereg.hyp.time}}) →
`DEVIATIONS.md` (every change, including failed hypotheses) → `HYPOTHESIS_V2.md` (v2 and its forward test, frozen
before the forward window; Amendment A5: the forward test was not run within the hackathon window) →
`results/oos_peeks.log` (each run that read held-out data, including reproductions and verifier runs) →
`results/provenance/experiments.json` (the experiment registry: every evaluation and every choice made after an OOS
look, which the paper's Appendix {{app:Records}} lists). The live paper session was stopped by a team decision and is
not used (`research/v2/maker/DEVIATIONS_LIVE.md` L15).

## Reproduce

```bash
bash run.sh all            # = setup, data, reproduce; no keys
bash run.sh setup          # .venv + requirements-repro.txt (--locked: requirements.lock) + tectonic   ~1-2 min
bash run.sh data           # public Polymarket APIs, no keys; resumable, cached in data/; ends with verify-inputs  ~35-120 min
bash run.sh verify-inputs  # data/ against results/provenance/inputs_manifest.json; exit 0 = the snapshot's inputs  ~1 min
bash run.sh reproduce      # bash reproduce.sh: the submitted snapshot, offline, fail-fast        ~1-1.5 h
bash run.sh fresh-fetch    # a NEW holdout from today's listing -> results/fresh_holdout_new/<utc>/ (network)
bash run.sh docs           # README.md, docs/DEVPOST.md, docs/COMPLIANCE.md from results/paper/numbers.json  ~1 s
```

Python 3.14 made `requirements.lock`; a clean run on HiPerGator used Python 3.12.5 (`module load python/3.12`; the
system `python3` there is 3.9). Every run records its Python, `pip freeze` and tectonic version in
`results/repro/run_manifest.json`.

`reproduce.sh` runs these stages; every step goes through `scripts/repro/run_step.py` (log in
`results/repro/logs/<step>.log`; a nonzero exit, or a declared output the step did not rewrite, stops the run):

| Stage | What runs |
|---|---|
| s00 inputs | `scripts/freeze_universe.py --check`, `scripts/repro/manifest.py verify` (universe, split, OOS start, every tape, archived inputs, frozen model), restore of the archived fresh-holdout window and factor files (`results/repro/inputs/`) |
| s01–s02 | `run_all.py --oos` (prints, H1–H6, calibration, tiers, fast tier → `results/summary.json`); `scripts/reproduce_inputs.py` (IS jump table and lowloss feature tables, rebuilt when their code or inputs changed) |
| s03 | v2: `scripts/v2_causal.py` (IS and OOS, with ½- and 1-tick slippage), `scripts/v2_cost_stress.py`, `scripts/note_metrics.py`; the corrected producers `scripts/v2_strict.py --oos` (strict timing labels, executable copier → `results/v2/strict_causal.json`) and `scripts/cv_causal_points.py --oos` (causal every-point CV book → `results/tier0/causal_points.json`) |
| s04 | figures and descriptive tables: `v2_figures.py`, `factor_regression.py`, `leverage_stats.py`, `paper_figures.py`, `rally_gate_eval.py`, `data_coverage.py` |
| s05 | risk and capacity: `v2_wallet_cap.py --is` / `--oos --repro`, `impact_model.py` (only when the live recordings in `data/live` exist; otherwise a recorded skip and the committed `results/liquidity/impact.json`), `edge_persistence.py` |
| s06 | `psr_mintrl.py` (PSR, MinTRL, copier fill stress), `cv_cost_turnover.py` |
| s07 | `sponsor_evidence.py` (fails unless the DuckDB SQL recheck and the Vultr unit tests ran), `cv_teaser_fig.py` |
| s08 | the fresh holdout rerun on its archived inputs with the network disabled (`scripts/repro/holdout_inputs.py run-fixed`), `firm_scenario_fig.py` |
| s09 | `redteam_stamp_lag.py`, `redteam_derived.py` |
| s10 | `build_paper.py` (exits nonzero, leaving `docs/NOTE.pdf` unreplaced, on a missing compiler, > 5 main pages, < 11 pt text, the honesty grep or a fact check: registry counts and labels as printed, executable results first), `build_docs.py` |
| s11 | `scripts/repro/artifacts.py check`: every source of `results/paper/numbers.json` was rewritten in this run or is a listed committed artifact with an unchanged sha256; `results/repro/run_manifest.json` |

Things to know before running it:
- **Snapshot, not a refetch.** Python steps run with `COURTSIDE_OFFLINE=1`: a connection to any non-local host fails
  the step. Tape drift from a later crawl stops the run; `ALLOW_INPUT_DRIFT=1` runs anyway and the run manifest says
  the inputs are not the snapshot's. The fresh holdout fetched on 2026-10-04 at 05:44 UTC (22 matches) is archived
  with its window listing; a refetch lists different matches and is a new evaluation (`bash run.sh fresh-fetch`).
- **Held-out re-reads.** Steps that re-read the OOS period log a line before reading. Under `reproduce.sh` those lines
  go to `results/repro/reads.log` (untracked), and the committed `results/oos_peeks.log` is left unchanged. Run
  outside `reproduce.sh`, such scripts append to `results/oos_peeks.log` (`git checkout results/oos_peeks.log`
  removes the lines); those lines record your run, not new decisions. The paper's counts of evaluations and of
  choices made after an OOS look come from `results/provenance/experiments.json`, not from the log's length.
- **Frozen universe.** Polymarket's public event list keeps growing (a crawl late on 2026-10-03 also returns matches
  that started that day after ours). `bash run.sh data` runs `scripts/freeze_universe.py`, which pins the cached
  event list to the {{univ.matches}} condition ids in `results/universe_conds.txt.gz`; `reproduce.sh` checks it.
- **Committed artifacts.** `results/paper/committed_artifacts.json` lists every paper source `reproduce.sh` does not
  recompute, with its producer, sha256 and why (HiPerGator jobs such as the latency sweep and ball tracking, the
  capacity grid, the blind out-of-universe tests evaluated once, recordings of live books). A reproduction fails if
  one of them changed without its producer running.
- **Live recordings cannot be re-downloaded.** The order-book and score-feed recordings of 2026-10-03 behind the
  latency, depth and replay numbers were made with `src/live_recorder.py` and live in `data/live*` (gitignored); the
  derived numbers are committed in `results/` and `research/v2/{latency,livefill,blocklag}/`.
- **Checking the numbers.** A run that finishes shows the steps ran; it does not show the numbers match. Compare
  against a reference captured outside the checkout:
  `.venv/bin/python scripts/check_paper_reproduction.py --reference <reference.json> --report <report.json>`
  (every printed value exact, raw values to 1e-8 absolute / 1e-10 relative, frozen assets and PDF provenance).
- **The blind forward test was not run** (`HYPOTHESIS_V2.md` A5: pre-registered, not run within the hackathon window;
  `results/forward_peeks.log` has no START line). `scripts/forward_test.py` is a one-shot that logs every run; if
  `results/v2/forward.json` ever exists, `bash run.sh reproduce` fills the one slot in the paper, this README and the
  Devpost text from it.

## Other commands

| Command | What |
|---|---|
| `bash run.sh setup --full` | also installs `requirements-extra.txt`: tracking (torch, OpenCV, ONNX Runtime) and the deck |
| `bash run.sh engine` | the paper-only COURTSIDE engine: order books on the committed sample, then 60 s of live public books |
| `bash run.sh cv` | the ball-tracking call engine on the held-out OpenTTGames clip (checks the frozen call model's sha256 first) |
| `bash run.sh money` | terminal replay of the v2 in-sample backtest with a paper-money counter (after `reproduce`) |
| `bash run.sh dashboard` | read-only dashboard at http://localhost:8765 |
| `bash run.sh live` | the paper trader on live public books, read-only (a tool; the pre-registered live session was stopped and is not used) |
| `python scripts/forward_test.py --start <UTC> --end <UTC>` | the frozen v2 rule on any window (the pre-registered forward test was not run: `HYPOTHESIS_V2.md` A5) |
| `sbatch hpg/track_*.sbatch`, `sbatch hpg/tennis_*.sbatch` | table-tennis and tennis tracking on HiPerGator (`src/tracking/README.md`, `src/tennis_tracking/README.md`) |
| `research/v2/<lens>/` | six optimisation lenses, each with two adversarial verifier reports |

## Layout

| path | what |
|---|---|
| `src/polymarket.py`, `src/tape.py` | public API client; universe, locked 80/20 split by match count, side-of-book classification |
| `src/tiers.py`, `src/fasttier.py` | markouts by seconds since the score event; the walk-forward fast tier (H6) |
| `src/v2.py` | the frozen v2 rule, runnable on any period |
| `src/markov.py` | exact point-level tennis Markov model (fair value, leverage) |
| `src/paper.py` | replays recorded live books; orders wait the venue delay plus latency, then walk the book |
| `engine/` | paper-only engine: v2 risk limits, $1,000 daily stop, kill switches (`engine/risk/limits.py`) |
| `src/tracking/`, `src/tennis_tracking/`, `engine/vision/` | ball tracking and the causal call engine |
| `results/` | every reported number; `results/paper/numbers.json` maps each paper number to its source |
| `docs/paper/` | the LaTeX source of `docs/NOTE.pdf` |
| `docs/templates/` | the templates of this README, the Devpost text and the compliance checklist |

## Data, sources and licences

- **Market data:** Polymarket Gamma, Data and CLOB APIs and its sports websocket; the Kalshi public market-data API.
  Public, no keys. Score feeds for the latency study: ESPN's public scoreboard and the WTA public API, read live;
  only derived timings are committed.
- **Factors:** Kenneth R. French Data Library (Fama–French market, size, value; momentum).
- **Video:** OpenTTGames (OSAI, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0); the table-tennis clips are derived from it under the same licence.
  The real tennis rally in the video is {{meta:tennis_credit}}; source, licence terms and hashes in
  `results/viz/v60_assets/tennis_real/LICENSE.md`. Narration and music bed: AI-generated with {{meta:voice}}. The TrackNet
  tennis dataset (Huang et al. 2019) is used for evaluation only; no broadcast frames are included.
- **Pre-existing components** (not built during the event; disclosed per the Terms §14.2): BlurBall pretrained
  weights and code (MIT) on WASB-SBDT (MIT), used zero-shot for table-tennis ball detection; TrackNet weights and
  TennisProject / TennisCourtDetector code (no licence file; used unmodified for evaluation, not vendored or
  redistributed); in the video, a licensed stock tennis clip, {{meta:tennis_credit}}, and an AI voice and music bed
  from {{meta:voice}}. Everything else was written during the event, with AI coding assistants.
- No API keys or licensed raw data are committed; raw data lives in `data/` (gitignored). The code only reads public
  data and never places an order.
